81
00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:20.500
Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): But here's the key. DIDs themselves don't handle routing. They don't deliver your messages. Instead, service endpoints connect your DID world to existing infrastructure, like the internet, peer-to-peer networks, or even email.

82
00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:32.919
Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): That's how messages actually get from point A to point B. So think of service endpoints as the bridge. The keys in your DID prove who you are, but the service endpoints tell others how to find you and which communication channels to use.

